1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,340
 Residents in Côte d'Ange NDG have elected a new borough mayor.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,520
 Stephanie Valenzuela captured just half, 50% of the vote,

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:09,700
 defeating incumbent Grasso-Kissouki-Katawa.

4
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:12,420
 The new borough council is made up of three councillors

5
00:00:12,420 --> 00:00:15,140
 from Ensemble Montréal and two from Projet Montréal.

6
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,340
 Stephanie Valenzuela joins us now.

7
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:18,760
 Good morning. Congratulations.

8
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,160
 Good morning. Thank you for having me.

9
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:21,900
 How are you feeling?

10
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:29,520
 To be honest, still really overwhelmed with the support

11
00:00:29,520 --> 00:00:31,640
 I've been receiving in the last few days and the messages,

12
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:34,580
 but feeling very good and very proud of the work

13
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:36,020
 that we put in during this campaign.

14
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:38,160
 What do you think contributed to your win?

15
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:42,840
 Oh, really, it's the door knocking and the meeting the residents

16
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:49,100
 and hearing everyone over the last 42 days of this campaign.

17
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,800
 But even before that, when we announced our complete team in August,

18
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:56,400
 I've been a sitting councillor for the District of Darlington

19
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,620
 for the last four years.

20
00:00:57,620 --> 00:01:02,460
 And for me, in this mandate, I really learned the importance

21
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:05,400
 of meeting with residents, hearing them out.

22
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:06,380
 What are the grievances?

23
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:08,880
 What are the issues they'd like to resolve?

24
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:12,240
 And that's really what I took with me along this campaign.

25
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:15,760
 How to listen to people, how to bring solutions.

26
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:19,640
 And I think with that, the results are there.

27
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:23,300
 It shows that that's exactly what we did in this campaign.

28
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:26,320
 So let's talk about solutions and the next four years.

29
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,120
 What are your top priorities for the borough?

30
00:01:28,820 --> 00:01:31,800
 Yeah, well, we were very clear from the very beginning

31
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:35,520
 when we announced our local team and our campaign.

32
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:39,540
 We are very focused on bringing back basic services in our borough,

33
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:42,440
 taking care of the development of housing

34
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,720
 and the preservation of our housing stock in the borough,

35
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:48,500
 making sure that we stay affordable as much as possible.

36
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:52,740
 And of course, you know, security has always been top of mind

37
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:54,080
 in the borough of Kud and Ajendiji.

38
00:01:54,280 --> 00:01:57,740
 So these are three, you know, axes that are very clear to us

39
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,380
 that we want to make sure we prioritize.

40
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:03,280
 But at this very moment, it's the budget of 2026

41
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:05,080
 that we're already starting to work on

42
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:08,600
 to make sure that we have these priorities in there.

43
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:11,540
 Let's talk about developing the housing stock.

44
00:02:11,660 --> 00:02:14,720
 One of the places where that housing stock will be developed

45
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:17,200
 is in the Namuribidrom site.

46
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,680
 Where do you think stand with that?

47
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:24,700
 So there was two social off-market projects

48
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:27,120
 that were adopted in the last council

49
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,940
 with the council that we had, you know,

50
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:31,900
 prior to the campaign and to the election.

51
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:34,700
 So that's already something that's on the table.

52
00:02:35,020 --> 00:02:38,060
 It's clear that we need to continue discussions

53
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:39,340
 with all levels of government

54
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:41,700
 to see how the rest of the Namuribidrom site

55
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,520
 will be developed.

56
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,820
 There was federal funding that came in

57
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:46,540
 just a few months ago.

58
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,440
 So there's a whole conversation.

59
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:52,080
 And, you know, Claude Pinard was elected in Saint-Jacques.

60
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:56,040
 There's potentially a lot of different scenarios

61
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,420
 that are going to come in with recounting across the city.

62
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:01,840
 But we have a plan and we have every intention

63
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:03,360
 of working with all the stakeholders,

64
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:06,320
 including the Galo and the local stakeholders

65
00:03:06,320 --> 00:03:07,580
 that we have here in the borough.

66
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:11,720
 What about the existing stock in Côte d'Inege and DG?

67
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:14,160
 I know that there are some buildings,

68
00:03:14,300 --> 00:03:15,280
 some municipal housing buildings

69
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,700
 that are not being used right now.

70
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:18,900
 Are there any plans to do something about that?

71
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,060
 There are definitely plans to do something with that.

72
00:03:22,140 --> 00:03:23,740
 That was something that was also announced

73
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:28,700
 as one of our, you know, campaign engagements with Soraya.

74
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,840
 But I'll give you a very concrete example

75
00:03:30,840 --> 00:03:32,340
 of something that needs to advance

76
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:35,820
 just in terms of local housing stock.

77
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:39,180
 There's a project called Project Chester on Walkley.

78
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:42,200
 It has been abandoned since, I believe, 2012.

79
00:03:43,620 --> 00:03:46,760
 There's potential to already start working on that project.

80
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:49,160
 And so we need to prioritize that.

81
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,360
 So that's one of the first things

82
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:53,120
 that I'm going to be doing coming into my seat

83
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,940
 as a borough mayor is to make sure

84
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:56,880
 that we can finally advance on this project.

85
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,660
 If there's money that is missing,

86
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:00,860
 if there's, you know, funding that is needed,

87
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,220
 we need to find a way to work

88
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:03,040
 with our different partners

89
00:04:03,040 --> 00:04:04,780
 to finally advance on this project.

90
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:07,080
 Another thing that was talked about

91
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,600
 during the campaign was extending Cavendish.

92
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:10,760
 Yes.

93
00:04:12,260 --> 00:04:15,480
 What's the plan going forward with that?

94
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:19,540
 Well, as we had announced just a few weeks ago already,

95
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:21,380
 towards the tail end of the campaign,

96
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:25,180
 our intention coming into this mandate

97
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,300
 is to make sure that we go forward

98
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:30,340
 with Cavendish Extension by deposing

99
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,900
 our intentions through the BAP.

100
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:34,980
 The BAP will have to analyze it.

101
00:04:35,060 --> 00:04:37,100
 That's where the last administration had stopped

102
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:38,940
 in terms of going forward with the project.

103
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:41,140
 The BAP will determine the cost.

104
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:43,680
 You know, it will determine the actual way

105
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,980
 that we can do this in a way

106
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:48,280
 that is not hopefully detrimental to the environment.

107
00:04:48,680 --> 00:04:50,960
 So we want to put that on the table,

108
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,440
 understand the feasibility

109
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,160
 of putting in the Cavendish Extension.

110
00:04:54,560 --> 00:04:56,100
 But I think for us, our party,

111
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,140
 it's been very clear

112
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,280
 that if we're going to develop

113
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,280
 an entire site,

114
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:00,680
 like the Numero Hippodrome site,

115
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:01,920
 we need to make sure

116
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:04,340
 that accessibility is included,

117
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:05,560
 security is included.

118
00:05:05,900 --> 00:05:07,440
 And with the SIM,

119
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,780
 it was very clear

120
00:05:08,780 --> 00:05:11,020
 that you cannot develop

121
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:13,560
 a site with over 10,000 units

122
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,700
 and so much circulation

123
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:16,360
 and people going through

124
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,600
 if you don't have different access points

125
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,960
 that are safe and secure

126
00:05:19,960 --> 00:05:20,800
 to enter the area.

127
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,680
 So we're very clear on that.

128
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,320
 The SIM being

129
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,740
 the Montreal Fire Department, correct?

130
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:25,880
 Exactly, yes.

131
00:05:26,080 --> 00:05:27,560
 And I'm curious to know,

132
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:28,800
 because you're talking about feasibility,

133
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,600
 if it came to that,

134
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,700
 do you see a scenario

135
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:34,120
 where you would ask

136
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,300
 Coat St. Luke

137
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,360
 or Town of Mount Royal

138
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:36,960
 to contribute?

139
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,020
 Well, they've always been

140
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,720
 very close collaborators

141
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:42,860
 on this intention.

142
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:43,760
 My colleague,

143
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:44,840
 Alan de Souza

144
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:45,860
 from Saint-Laurent

145
00:05:45,860 --> 00:05:47,260
 had been working with them

146
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,140
 for over, you know, decades.

147
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:51,040
 So if it comes to a point

148
00:05:51,040 --> 00:05:52,080
 where we have to sit down

149
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:52,900
 and discuss further,

150
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,280
 then for sure we will do that.

151
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:54,860
 But for now,

152
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,280
 we have to focus on

153
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,920
 the first step,

154
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:58,640
 which is deposing

155
00:05:58,640 --> 00:05:59,560
 this project at the BAP.

156
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:00,200
 All right.

157
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:01,880
 Homelessness is an issue

158
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:04,460
 that you will have to deal with

159
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:06,460
 and so all the elected officials

160
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:07,180
 at City Hall

161
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:08,020
 are going to have to deal with.

162
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,280
 Let's talk about specifically,

163
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:09,500
 though,

164
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:10,780
 Côte d'Aige, NDG.

165
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:13,160
 I know in the last few years

166
00:06:13,160 --> 00:06:15,040
 there have been some concerns

167
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:17,040
 in Martin Luther King Park.

168
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,480
 What's the solution

169
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,360
 that you're proposing

170
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:20,860
 and where do you go from there?

171
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:23,220
 Yeah, thank you for the question.

172
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,540
 Actually, it's been a priority for me

173
00:06:25,540 --> 00:06:27,040
 even as a sitting councillor.

174
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:28,880
 So one of the first things

175
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:29,660
 that we're going to do,

176
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:30,380
 you know,

177
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,900
 it's the month of November.

178
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,940
 In a few weeks,

179
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:33,580
 we're going to start

180
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:34,560
 to feel the cold

181
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,360
 in a much different way

182
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,640
 like we do every winter.

183
00:06:38,020 --> 00:06:39,360
 So we need to work

184
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,560
 with the stakeholders.

185
00:06:40,780 --> 00:06:41,500
 We need to find out

186
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,600
 what was already planned

187
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:44,020
 with this previous administration

188
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:45,560
 and what do we need to do

189
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,660
 to adjust to make sure

190
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:48,620
 that nobody is found

191
00:06:48,620 --> 00:06:49,560
 in the park

192
00:06:49,560 --> 00:06:52,060
 at minus 20 degrees, right?

193
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:53,200
 So one of the things

194
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:54,360
 that I was able to do

195
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,800
 in my last mandate

196
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:56,760
 as a city councillor

197
00:06:56,760 --> 00:06:57,660
 was depose a motion

198
00:06:57,660 --> 00:07:00,620
 and get services put in

199
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:01,920
 through the partnership

200
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,840
 with a local community organization.

201
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:05,420
 So that exists right now.

202
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,100
 What we need to know is,

203
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:07,320
 you know,

204
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,020
 how many people

205
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:09,500
 have been using that site,

206
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:10,220
 how many people

207
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,940
 are currently in the borough

208
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:13,380
 that need to be redirected

209
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,040
 to resources

210
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:14,700
 to make sure

211
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:15,620
 that we can identify

212
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,540
 where they all are.

213
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:17,800
 And again,

214
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,260
 my team with

215
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:19,860
 Ensemble Montréal

216
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:20,440
 and Soraya

217
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,440
 had proposed

218
00:07:21,440 --> 00:07:22,800
 a lot of measures

219
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,720
 for the whole city of Montreal

220
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:25,900
 when it comes to homelessness.

221
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,320
 So there's going to be work

222
00:07:27,320 --> 00:07:28,120
 that we need to do

223
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:28,740
 all together

224
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:29,360
 to make sure

225
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,920
 that these programs

226
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,960
 and these envelopes

227
00:07:31,960 --> 00:07:32,440
 trickle down

228
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:33,480
 to all the different boroughs

229
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:34,400
 that are impacted

230
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,500
 in a different way

231
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:37,620
 with vulnerable populations.

232
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:38,980
 One of the other

233
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,680
 big projects

234
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,640
 from the Projet Montréal era

235
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:43,020
 specifically in Cote d'Anege,

236
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:43,500
 NDG,

237
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,460
 was the Terrebonne bike path.

238
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:46,320
 I'm curious to know

239
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:47,160
 what happens to that.

240
00:07:47,220 --> 00:07:48,220
 Will it stay open this winter?

241
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,940
 So like we said,

242
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:52,440
 we're going to go into an audit.

243
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,960
 So until that audit is done,

244
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:55,160
 That's not happening anymore though.

245
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,660
 That audit's not happening anymore.

246
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:59,120
 It's not that it's not happening.

247
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,680
 It's we have to get access

248
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,320
 to the audit

249
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,400
 that was already prepared

250
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,480
 by the administration.

251
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:04,560
 We're going to take a look

252
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:05,120
 at that audit

253
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,260
 and see what was

254
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,880
 the evaluation of it.

255
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,080
 And depending on

256
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:10,980
 the results of it

257
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,000
 and the access to it,

258
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:12,800
 then potentially

259
00:08:12,800 --> 00:08:14,160
 we might not have another audit

260
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:14,840
 and we would use

261
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:15,800
 the results of that audit.

262
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,260
 But I think what's important

263
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:18,580
 is that there was already

264
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,900
 something that was done

265
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:20,780
 that was paid for

266
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:21,540
 by taxpayers.

267
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,080
 And there is

268
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,840
 potentially

269
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:24,900
 some solutions

270
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:26,480
 to how we can improve

271
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:28,000
 and modify

272
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,100
 the current network

273
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,060
 that's there.

274
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:32,520
 So the current position

275
00:08:32,520 --> 00:08:33,140
 for us

276
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:33,600
 is that

277
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:34,820
 we wait

278
00:08:34,820 --> 00:08:35,820
 for the results.

279
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,120
 We keep

280
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:37,780
 what is there

281
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:38,420
 as a network.

282
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:39,140
 So the maintenance

283
00:08:39,140 --> 00:08:40,060
 of the Taoban

284
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:41,360
 is still very much

285
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:43,380
